<title>USA: Georgia Power Hatch 1 power unit at 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power Hatch 1 power unit at 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co's 741 megawatt (MW) Hatch 1 nuclear power unit has restarted and was operating at 30 percent power early this morning, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Baxley, Ga., was take off line last Wednesday when a small leak was found in a three-quarter inch diameter line inside the drywell building that houses the reactor.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 765 MW, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>Georgia Power is a subsidiary of Southern Co.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
